# File: scripts/__tests__/start-issue-controller.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/449-report-closed-issues-at-start-as-issue-closed-instead-of-issue-unreadable/requirements.md
Feature: Report closed issues at START as issue_closed instead of issue_unreadable

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Closed issue is reported as closed
    Given "gh issue view 42" succeeds and returns issue 42 with state "CLOSED"
    When START runs for issue 42
    Then ".omp/sdlc/handoffs/42-start.json" has status "failed", reasonCode "issue_closed", summary "GitHub issue #42 is CLOSED", intervention true, step "start", and next null
    And the issue view is the only command START ran

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Unreadable issue is unchanged
    Given "gh issue view 42" fails, returns unparseable output, returns issue 41, or returns issue 42 without a state
    When START runs for issue 42
    Then ".omp/sdlc/handoffs/42-start.json" has reasonCode "issue_unreadable" and summary "GitHub issue #42 is unreadable"
    And the issue view is the only command START ran

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Open issue is unchanged
    Given "gh issue view 42" succeeds and returns issue 42 with state "OPEN" and no open blocker
    When START runs for issue 42
    Then it reads the official blocked-by graph, develops branch "42-ship-it", and writes a passed handoff with next "implement"
